FINDINGS (evidence only; product code was not edited)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
F1 BLOCKER (product, coursebook/generation.py): every lesson/validation request is built with
   timeout_s=60.0 (build_lesson_request / build_lesson_validation_request, no env override), and
   _call_llm raises ProviderTimeout when the returned call took longer than that declared
   deadline. The host call returned after 115.8 s, so the job failed. On this provider the
   lesson stage cannot be relied on to stay under 60 s per call (observed 14.2 s - 115.8 s).
F2 BLOCKER (product, coursebook/generation.py CostBudget): max_calls defaults to 8 per job, but a
   5-section plan needs lesson+validation per section (>=10 calls) and validation rejects add a
   retry call each. Even without F1 this plan would end POLICY_VIOLATION "job already made 8
   provider calls (ceiling 8)" — the exact error recorded earlier on this home for
   job_06388582367a40af8c69d01dd9c3964a (2026-11-06T15:46:11Z).
F3 HARNESS (scripts/cb011-parent-probe.py): `full`/`approve` never send expected_revision to
   parent.final.approve, so the probe cannot reach the final approval state it exists to prove.
F4 MAPPING (coursebook/job_service.py _error_code): ProviderTimeout is reported as
   GRADER_UNAVAILABLE, which points a reader at the grader instead of the provider deadline.

CONSEQUENCE FOR THIS CARD: the expected sequence stopped at the lesson stage. Final approval and
export are NOT proven; no PDF exists for this course. No retry with a fresh course was made.
